{"name":"Grey Werewolf","hex":"#625f5c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"werewolf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is transformed or can transform into a wolf or a wolflike human, often said to do so during a full moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/werewolf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Werewolf","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a werewolf, or occasionally lycanthrope, is an individual who can shapeshift into a wolf or therianthropic hybrid wolf–humanlike creature, either voluntarily or involuntarily due to a curse or other affliction. In modern fiction, especially film, transformations are often depicted as triggered by the full moon and transmitted by a bite or scratch from another werewolf. Early sources for belief in this ability or affliction, called lycanthropy, are Petronius (27–66) and Gervase of Tilbury (1150–1228)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/WeirdTalesv36n2pg038_The_Werewolf_Howls.png/330px-WeirdTalesv36n2pg038_The_Werewolf_Howls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werewolf","wikidata":"Q9410"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg/500px-Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg/1280px-Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg/500px-Lekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dolon wearing a wolfskin. Attic red-figure vase, c. 460 BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALekythos_Dolon_Louvre_CA1802.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg/500px-Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg/1280px-Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg/500px-Lycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zeus turning Lycaon into a wolf, engraving by Hendrik Goltzius.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALycaon_Transformed_into_a_Wolf_LACMA_M.71.76.9.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Bronspl%C3%A5t_pressbleck_%C3%96land_vendeltid.jpg/500px-Bronspl%C3%A5t_pressbleck_%C3%96land_vendeltid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped